-- title:
--   The level Γ_H(q²M') q-expansion field is finite over a rational subfield
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the non-units of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` for the residue field of $A$. Let $H =$ `levelH q M'` be the kernel of the reduction homomorphism $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that is the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, and let $\Gamma_H(q^2M') \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ be the associated congruence subgroup, the preimage of $H$ under the determinant-of-diagonal character on $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$. Let $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')\,H$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with coefficients in $\kappa$. The assertion is that there exists an element $t \in E$ such that $E$ is a finite-dimensional vector space over the subfield $\kappa(t)$ obtained by adjoining $t$ to $\kappa$ inside $E$.
--
--   This records that the characteristic-$q$ $q$-expansion field of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, is a function field in one variable over its algebraically closed constant field $\kappa$. It is used downstream to identify valuation subrings of this field containing $\kappa$ with places, and hence in the analysis of places, rationality and integral models on the semistable specialisation of the full-level curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_finiteDimensional_adjoin_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH.lean

